{"title":"Career Roadmap · Automation Technician","role":"Automation Technician","summary":"An Automation Technician installs, configures, tests, troubleshoots, and maintains automated machines, industrial control systems, sensors, PLCs, robotics, and connected equipment.","facts":{"Current degree":"BCA (Bachelor of Computer Applications)","Course":"BCA – IoT / Robotics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Typical route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BCA IoT/Robotics","IoT/Automation Internship","Automation Technician / Controls Technician","Senior Automation Technician","Automation Engineer / Controls Engineer","Automation Lead"]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A BCA graduate can enter automation technician roles, particularly where the work involves IoT, software, industrial networking, monitoring, testing, and basic controls. For deeply electrical/industrial-control-heavy roles, employers may prefer Diploma/B.Tech backgrounds in Electrical, Electronics, Instrumentation, Mechatronics, or Automation."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Industry Direction","What the Technician Should Build"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2028"},{"text":"Industrial IoT, smart manufacturing, robotics"},{"text":"PLC, sensors, electronics, industrial networking"}],[{"text":"2028–2030"},{"text":"Connected factories and predictive maintenance"},{"text":"SCADA, MQTT, Modbus, OPC UA, Python"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"AI-assisted automation"},{"text":"Machine vision, edge AI, predictive analytics"}],[{"text":"2033–2036"},{"text":"Autonomous production systems"},{"text":"Robotics, digital twins, advanced controls"}],[{"text":"2036–2040"},{"text":"Human-machine collaboration"},{"text":"Collaborative robots, AI monitoring, autonomous systems"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Intelligent autonomous factories"},{"text":"AI-driven industrial operations and robotics"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Key Skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Computing + electronics foundation"},{"text":"Python, C, Linux, basic electronics, Arduino"},{"text":"IoT sensor project"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Automation foundation"},{"text":"Sensors, actuators, PLC basics, GPIO, communication protocols"},{"text":"PLC/Arduino automation project"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Industrial automation"},{"text":"PLC programming, SCADA, HMI, Modbus, MQTT, industrial networking"},{"text":"Automated production-line project"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Industry readiness"},{"text":"Robotics, troubleshooting, IIoT, dashboards, predictive maintenance"},{"text":"Industrial automation capstone + internship"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Computing & Electronics Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"C fundamentals"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Basic Java"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"OOP fundamentals"},{"text":"Data structures"},{"text":"File handling"},{"text":"Exception handling"},{"text":"Git/GitHub"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Python is especially useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sensor data processing"},{"text":"Automation scripts"},{"text":"Device monitoring"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Predictive maintenance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Linux"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linux command line"},{"text":"Files and permissions"},{"text":"Processes"},{"text":"Networking basics"},{"text":"SSH"},{"text":"Shell scripting"},{"text":"Package management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Linux becomes increasingly important in IoT gateways, edge computing and industrial systems."},{"type":"h","text":"3. Electronics Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Voltage/current/resistance"},{"text":"Ohm's law"},{"text":"Digital vs analog signals"},{"text":"Resistors/capacitors"},{"text":"Transistors"},{"text":"Relays"},{"text":"LEDs"},{"text":"Diodes"},{"text":"Power supplies"},{"text":"ADC/DAC concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Microcontrollers"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arduino"},{"text":"ESP32"},{"text":"Raspberry Pi"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Temperature","Sensor","ESP32","Wi-Fi","Dashboard"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — IoT & Automation Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Sensors"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"Humidity"},{"text":"Pressure"},{"text":"Proximity"},{"text":"Ultrasonic"},{"text":"Infrared"},{"text":"Light"},{"text":"Motion"},{"text":"Current"},{"text":"Voltage"},{"text":"Gas sensors"},{"text":"Encoders"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sensor","Controller","Actuator","Feedback"]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Actuators"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DC motors"},{"text":"Servo motors"},{"text":"Stepper motors"},{"text":"Solenoids"},{"text":"Relays"},{"text":"Motor drivers"},{"text":"Pneumatic actuator concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. PLC Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"PLC knowledge is one of the most important additions for an automation technician."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PLC architecture"},{"text":"Digital inputs/outputs"},{"text":"Analog inputs/outputs"},{"text":"Ladder Logic"},{"text":"Timers"},{"text":"Counters"},{"text":"Comparators"},{"text":"Latching"},{"text":"Interlocks"},{"text":"Alarms"},{"text":"Basic PID concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the basic architecture:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sensor","PLC","Logic","Actuator","Feedback"]},{"type":"h","text":"4. HMI"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how operators interact with machines through:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Start/st